## 5.3 📌 Topic Recap & Important Things to Remember (Rapid Revision Checklist)

- ✅ BST is a **binary tree with the ordering property** — left child < parent < right child.
- ✅ **In-order traversal** of a BST yields **sorted order** — the heart of using BST as a dictionary.
- ✅ **Insert** and **Search** are both $O(\log n)$ average, $O(n)$ worst-case (skewed).
- ✅ **Deletion has 3 cases**: leaf, one child, two children (use in-order successor).
- ✅ **In-order successor** = leftmost node of right sub-tree.
- ✅ **In-order predecessor** = rightmost node of left sub-tree.
- ✅ **strcmp()** returns `0` for equal, negative if first < second, positive if first > second.
- ✅ **Balanced BST** (AVL/Red-Black) guarantees $O(\log n)$ — preferred for production.
- ✅ Always **free the entire tree** before program exit to avoid memory leaks.
- ✅ Always **assign the return value of `insert` and `deleteNode`** back to `root`.
- ✅ KTU 2024 lab evaluation checks: (1) compilable code, (2) correct I/O, (3) viva on complexity, (4) memory cleanup, (5) edge-case handling (empty tree, duplicates, deletion of root).

